# Pairs with RNoStrandedPrepare. The ordering a terminal waits for is taken
# over every prepare the saga wrote rather than over the prepares still
# outstanding, and one participant's prepare is never shipped - trimmed from the
# origin's WAL before it was read, or filtered out. The terminal then waits
# forever for a prepare that will never arrive, and every bucket the receiver
# did stage is stranded behind it. This is the wedge a shipper-side terminal
# hold (the #4480 remedy) must not have: it may wait only on records that exist.
# The base's guard is stated over outstanding records, which is why it cannot
# wedge.
#
# DEADLOCK: off is required: the wedged terminals are the only records left
# and none is deliverable, so the mutant always reaches a state with no enabled
# action, and with the check on TLC reports that first.
MODULE: RNoStrandedPrepareHoldWaitsOnUnshippedPrepare
TARGET: RNoStrandedPrepare
CLASS: Temporal
DEADLOCK: off
SUMMARY: a terminal waits on every prepare the saga wrote, including one never shipped, so it is never released
PERTURBS: OriginPrepare, DeliverTerminal

--- FIND
    /\ outbox' = outbox \cup {Prep(k) : k \in XKeys}
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: k2's prepare is never shipped (trimmed or filtered).
    /\ outbox' = outbox \cup {Prep(k) : k \in XKeys \ {k2}}
--- END
--- FIND
    /\ \A p \in outbox : (p.type = "prep" /\ p.key = m.key) => p \in dlv
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the terminal waits on every prepare of the saga, shipped or not.
    /\ \A k \in XKeys : Prep(k) \in dlv
--- END
